# RAG pipeline (`packages/server/app`)

Flow: `rag/parse.py` (txt/md/csv/pdf/docx → text) → `rag/chunk.py` (splits the guideline on
section headings, then LangChain `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter`, ~900 / 150) →
`rag/embed.py` (local Ollama `/api/embed`) → `rag/store.py` (writes chunks + an embedded document
catalogue to Chroma) → `rag/retrieve.py` (Chroma HNSW, cosine) → `rag/agent.py` (LangGraph
retrieve → rewrite loop) → `rag/generate.py` → `rag/profile.py`.

## Rules

- Keep FastAPI in `main.py`; RAG logic stays under `app/rag/`.
- Pydantic models in `app/models.py` must stay aligned with `packages/client/src/contract.ts`.
  Nothing generates one from the other, so a field change needs both sides edited.
- API errors use `{ "error": string }` for **all** failures, including 422 validation errors
  (see the two exception handlers), not FastAPI's default `detail`.
- `store.search(question, top_k)` is the only retrieval entry point. Chroma fills short result
  lists with its nearest neighbours regardless of relevance, so `retrieve.search` drops every hit
  below `RETRIEVAL_MIN_SCORE`. Never fabricate scores, or off-topic questions turn into confident
  medical advice.
- The query reaches retrieval through `rag/agent.py` (LangGraph). The first attempt uses the user's
  literal question; if nothing clears the threshold the graph rewrites the query
  (`rag/rewrite.py`, LLM, up to `RETRIEVAL_MAX_REWRITES`, default 2) and retrieves again. The
  rewrite only rephrases — it must never add facts — and the graph still refuses with
  `NO_CONTEXT_ANSWER` when every attempt is empty. Do not "fix" a weak match by lowering the
  threshold: that readmits off-topic questions.
- Chroma returns a **distance**; `retrieve.search` converts with `1 - distance` and callers only
  ever see a similarity. Do not compare a distance to `MIN_SCORE`, and keep the conversion in one
  place.
- Embeddings come from Ollama only. Never pass an `embedding_function` to Chroma: the default one
  downloads a model, which breaks the "local model, no surprise network calls" requirement.
- The collection name is derived from `EMBEDDING_MODEL`. A different model has a different
  dimension and Chroma rejects mixed dimensions, so do not pin one collection name across models.
- `Chroma is the only state`: chunks in `chunks_*`, the document catalogue in `documents_*`.
  `DocumentStore.hydrate()` reloads the catalogue at startup. Never keep a second authoritative
  copy in memory or in a JSON file.
- Chunks stay section-scoped: the heading is kept in `chunk.text` and in metadata, so section
  names remain searchable and the LLM knows whether a passage is patient or operational.
- `generate.py` returns the passages it actually put in the prompt; `main.py` reports those as
  `sources`. Do not report the raw retrieval result.
- No relevant chunk above the threshold → `NO_CONTEXT_ANSWER` with **no** sources and `llm: null`.
  Never let the LLM answer from its own knowledge.
- Chat completions go through `rag/llm.py`. `LlmUnavailable` (no key) → 503,
  `LlmRequestError` (provider failure) → 502. There is no template fallback.
- Startup runs `preflight()`, which fails fast when Chroma is unreachable, the embedding model is
  missing, or no LLM key exists. Keep the error messages actionable.
- New file types: add them in `parse.py` and raise `Unsupported file type` for anything else.
- Python deps live in `pyproject.toml`; use `uv sync` / `uv run`.
